abi/levels: libvx's frozen ABI levels (ADR-0004 items 5 and 8).

Level 0 is the draft: nothing is here until 6e4f freezes level 1 at M6's
close. A freeze writes, for its level N:

  N.symbols    libvx.so's exports, sorted, one to a line: the build's
               usr/lib/libvx.symbols copied here. Each build compares the
               library it makes with the file for VX_ABI_LEVEL, and fails
               on any difference: a symbol missing breaks every program
               built for the level; a new one belongs to the next level,
               declared inside #if VX_TARGET_ABI >= N+1.

  N.behaviour  the behaviour suite's SHA-256, as ./build release prints it
               ("ABI   vx-abi N, behaviour suite ..."). The suite is
               build.c's BEHAVIOUR_SUITE: vxapitest and libvxtest, native
               programs against libvx.so, with their manifests and
               scenarios. ./build release refuses a suite that differs,
               unless docs/release-notes.md has a line

                 behaviour-suite: HASH

               beside what changed and what programs may now see.

The Swift libraries' baselines for the same level are abi/swift/<triple>
(ADR-0048 item 5).
